# Exhaustiveness: root-app's spec change (the catalog edit) plus private-app, which
# is affected but cannot render at all - so it contributes an error, not a resource.
expect:affected=2 changed=1 resources=+0,-0,~1 errors=1
# Identical fixture to private-chart-bump; the only difference is --repo-creds none.
# There, private-app renders and its ConfigMap shows the new chartVersion. Here no
# credentials are supplied, so fetching the chart from the in-cluster registry must
# FAIL. Succeeding would mean a chart downloaded under CLUSTER credentials satisfied
# an anonymous run: the end-to-end tripwire for the per-mode chart-cache scope.
#
# private-chart-bump is the ONLY case that fetches this chart, so it must run first
# for that to be true - cases run in sort order and "bump" < "unauth". The dependency
# is checked, not assumed: expected/private-chart-unauth/cache-precondition fails this
# case if charts/cluster is empty when its cached pass starts.
#
# It proves the pull was ATTEMPTED, not that authentication was enforced: without
# credentials there is also no insecure: "true" for the registry's self-signed cert,
# so the pull fails TLS verification before reaching auth. The wording after that
# prefix is Go's x509 and differs per platform, so normalize.sh collapses it - the
# prefix stays, so a DIFFERENT failure would still break this pin.
#
# KNOWN ENVIRONMENTAL FAILURE, deliberately not pinned: if 127.0.0.1.nip.io resolves
# away from loopback for a window (a rebind-protecting or filtering resolver, a
# proxy), the anonymous pull fails as "Forbidden" (TLS accepted, HTTP 403) and this
# pin breaks while bump's authenticated pulls may keep passing - observed
# intermittently on a dev machine. That is the machine's DNS, not argocdf: pin the
# name in /etc/hosts (see the README network note).
must:^# Application: private-app
must:^# Error: failed to render
must:failed to fetch helm chart private-app from 127\.0\.0\.1\.nip\.io:5317/charts
must:tls: failed to verify certificate: <platform-specific>$
# The temp destination helm was given must NOT appear: it is redacted argocdf-side,
# because a path that no longer exists is noise in a PR comment and rewrites the
# comment on every run. The review gate independently bans the placeholders that a
# leaked path would normalize to.
must:--destination \(temp dir\)
# The catalog change itself must still be attributed to the parent, and an app-level
# render error must stay report CONTENT: changed>0 keeps the exit code at 2.
must:^# Application: root-app
must:^\+        targetRevision: 0.2.0$
must:^# Applications changed: 1$
must:^# Errors: 1$
# A successful render would put the chart's own ConfigMap in the report. Its absence
# is the case: `chartVersion` appears in private-chart-bump and must not here.
must-not:^[-+]    chartVersion:
